SUMMARY:Walk: Gatineau Corridor Trail! 9KM
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!\n# 🌿 
 Gatineau Corridor Trail Walk\n\n### An Easy\, Flat Walk — Perfect for Ge
 tting Started\n\nWe'll begin near Kennedy Station and make our way through
  a series of small parks before connecting with the Gatineau Corridor Trai
 l. Along the way\, we'll pass through areas filled with wildflowers\, tall
  grasses\, and natural growth that give you a glimpse of what these spaces
  can look like when nature is allowed to take over a little. 🌼🌿\n\nT
 he city has changed the way some of these green spaces are maintained\, al
 lowing the grass and wildflowers to grow more naturally. Instead of perfec
 tly manicured lawns\, you'll see a much more colourful and natural landsca
 pe — a little reminder that sometimes the most beautiful parts of the ci
 ty are the ones we simply let grow.\n\nDon't forget to join our **WhatsApp
  Group – [CLICK HERE!](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)
 **\n\n***\n\n## 🚶‍♂️ What We'll Do\n\nWe'll start at the Dollar T
 ree and walk through the surrounding green spaces before joining the Gatin
 eau Corridor Trail.\n\nAlong the way we'll:\n\n* Walk through several smal
 l parks\n* Follow the mostly flat trail\n* Lots of wildflowers\n* Stop for
  a break around Eglinton & Victoria Park\n* Enjoy some conversation and ti
 me to get to know each other\n* Make our way back to where we started\n\nT
 he walk is approximately **2hrs** depending on the pace of the group.\nAnd
  remember — **you can leave at any time.**\nThere are multiple points al
 ong the route where you can make your own way home.\n\n***\n\n## ☀️ We
 ather & Expectations\n\nThis walk happens in typical Toronto weather condi
 tions.\nPlease dress appropriately for the weather and bring water\, espec
 ially during the warmer months.\nThis is one of our easier walks. If you'v
 e been wanting to start walking more but aren't sure you're ready for a lo
 nger or more challenging hike\, **this is a great place to begin.**\n\n***
 \n\n## 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** In front of the Do
 llar Tree Store\n🫎 I'll be wearing my Moose Hat.\n⏰ **Meetup Time: 11
 :00 AM**\nI will only wait 5 minutes.\n**Early is on time. On time is late
 .**\n🚗 **Parking:** There is parking available in the area.\n🚇 **Tra
 nsit:** We're also relatively close to Kennedy Station.\n\n🏁 **End Poin
 t:** Back at the Dollar Tree Store\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$5
  cash in person or e-transfer**\n📧 **[mathewmaclean@hotmail.com](mailto
 :mathewmaclean@hotmail.com)**\nThis fee helps support the group and allows
  us to continue organizing events throughout Toronto.\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 Wh
 at to Bring\n\n💧 Water\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🥨 A snack\n
 🧴 Sunscreen on sunny days\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis wa
 lk is especially great for:\n\n* People who are getting back into walking\
 n* Anyone looking for an easy trail\n* Beginners who aren't ready for a ch
 allenging hike\n* People who want to meet others while getting some fresh 
 air\n* Anyone who simply wants an easy Saturday/Sunday outing\n\nThe activ
 ity is the container. **The people you meet along the way are the real exp
 erience.**\n\n***\n\nREMEMBER: You're welcome to RSVP ahead of time or jus
 t show up on the day if you're unsure about your schedule.\nSometimes thin
 gs happen and events may need to be cancelled or changed\, so please keep 
 an eye on the event page for updates.\n\n👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\nQuest
 ions? Post on the event wall or email:\n**[torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail
 .com](mailto:torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com)**\n\n**Come for the easy
  trail.**\n**Stay for the conversation.**\n**Leave with a new connection 
 — and maybe a new friend.** 🌿💛
