SUMMARY:🌊 Hamilton Waterfront & 🌿 Cootes Paradise Trail Adventure- 2
  Meetup Times!
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!\n# 🌊 
 Hamilton Waterfront & Cootes Paradise Trail Adventure\n\nJoin us for a day
  outside Toronto as we head to Hamilton to explore the waterfront and the 
 beautiful trails of Cootes Paradise.\nWe'll begin along the Hamilton water
 front before making our way into Cootes Paradise\, where we'll trade city 
 streets for wooded paths\, natural scenery\, and a little bit of adventure
 .\n\nThere are some hills and sections of uneven trail\, so come prepared 
 to walk — but that's part of what makes this such a great day out.\nThis
  is a social adventure\, not a formal tour. We're here to explore somewher
 e different\, get some exercise\, enjoy the scenery\, and most importantly
 \, spend time together.\n\nDon't forget to join our **WhatsApp Group – [
 CLICK HERE!](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\
 n## 🚆 Getting to Hamilton\n\n### Meetup Location #1 — Toronto\n\n**Ou
 tside the Fairmont Royal York facing Front street. This will be the ONLY M
 eetup spot for this location.**\n**Meetup: 9:00AM...we will only wait 15mi
 ns**\n**Departure: 9:30 AM sharp**\nLook for me in my Moose Hat.\n\nWe'll 
 take the GO Train from Union Station to West Harbour GO Station.\nPlease b
 e on time. Once the train leaves\, you will not be able to catch up with t
 he group.\n**GO Train Cost:** Approximately $10 for the Weekend & Holiday 
 One-Day Pass.\nYou can get your pass a week before - [CLICK HERE!](https:/
 /www.gotransit.com/en/partners-and-promotions/weekend-passes-with-go)\n\n#
 ## Meetup Location #2 — Hamilton\n\n**Bayfront Park Parking Lot**\n200 H
 arbour Front Drive\nWe will meet near the flag polls.\n**Meetup: 11:00 AM*
 *\n**We leave for the walk at 11:15 AM.**\nIf you're driving or already in
  Hamilton\, this is the place to meet us.\n\n***\n\n## 🌿 The Walk\n\nWe
 'll explore the Hamilton waterfront before heading into Cootes Paradise.\n
 Expect:\n\n* Waterfront views\n* Forested trails\n* Natural scenery\n* Som
 e hills\n* A few uneven or off-road sections\n* Plenty of time to chat and
  enjoy the day\n\nThis isn't a race. We'll keep a steady pace\, but you sh
 ould be comfortable walking for several hours.\n\n***\n\n## 🍔 After the
  Walk\n\nAfter our hike\, we'll head over to **Hutch's Harbour Front** for
  some ice cream. You can join us for or you're welcome to head home whenev
 er you'd like.\n**Return GO Train:** We expect to catch either the **2:23 
 PM or 3:23 PM** train\, depending on how the day goes.\nYou are also welco
 me to stay in Hamilton longer and make your own way home later.\n\n***\n\n
 ## 💵 Meetup Fee\n\n**$5 cash in person or e-transfer**\n**[mathewmaclea
 n@hotmail.com](mailto:mathewmaclean@hotmail.com)**\nThis fee helps support
  the group and allows us to continue creating events like this.\n\n***\n\n
 ## 🎒 What to Bring\n\n* Water\n* Comfortable walking shoes\n* A snack\n
 * Sunscreen\n* Weather-appropriate clothing\n* Money for lunch and transpo
 rtation\n\n***\n\n### A Few Notes\n\nYou can RSVP in advance or decide on 
 the day if you're unsure about your schedule.\nSometimes things happen and
  events may need to be cancelled or changed\, so please keep an eye on the
  event page for updates.\nThis group is open to anyone who wants to get ou
 tside\, explore the city and surrounding areas\, and meet people along the
  way — whether you're single\, coupled\, new to Toronto\, or have lived 
 here your whole life.\nWe also host movies\, walks\, hikes\, arts & cultur
 e outings\, restaurants and more.\n\n**Organizer: Mathew**\nQuestions? Pos
 t on the event wall or email:\n**[torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com](mai
 lto:torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com)**\n\n## 🌈 The Point of the Day
 \n\nThe trail is the reason we get outside.\nThe adventure is the reason w
 e go somewhere different.\nBut the people are the reason we keep coming ba
 ck.\n**Come for the waterfront.**\n**Stay for the adventure.**\n**Leave wi
 th a new connection — and maybe a new friend.** 🌊🌿
