SUMMARY:🌿🚶‍♂️ YORK BELTLINE TRAIL & Brunch! 🍻🌿
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!\n# 🌿
 🚶‍♂️ YORK BELTLINE TRAIL & BRUNCH 🍻🌿\n\n**A Hidden Urban Tr
 ail\, Easy Walking & A Relaxing Summer Sunday**\nLooking for an easy way t
 o get outside after work?\n\nJoin us for a summer walk along the York Belt
 line Trail\, one of Toronto's hidden green corridors.\n\nBuilt on the rout
 e of the historic Belt Line Railway\, this peaceful trail offers a surpris
 ing escape from the city\, with mature trees\, birdsong\, and plenty of sh
 ade—all just steps from the subway.\nThis is an easy\, mostly flat walk 
 with no major hills\, making it perfect for anyone who wants to stretch th
 eir legs\, enjoy some fresh air\, and meet new people.\n\nAfter our walk\,
  we'll head over to **The Bull: A Firkin Pub** for brunch and a chance to 
 relax\, chat\, and get to know one another. After all\, the walk is just t
 he beginning—the conversations afterward are where friendships often sta
 rt.\n\n📲 Don't forget to join our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE!](ht
 tps://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 🚶‍♂
 ️ What We'll Do\n\nWe'll spend about **90 minutes** walking the York Bel
 tline Trail at a comfortable social pace.\nAlong the way we'll enjoy one o
 f Toronto's lesser-known walking trails\, share some conversation\, and un
 wind after the workday.\n\nWhen we finish\, anyone who would like to is we
 lcome to join us for brunch at **The Bull: A Firkin Pub**. You're also wel
 come to head home after the walk if you prefer.\n\n***\n\n## ☀️ Weathe
 r & Expectations\n\nThis walk happens rain or shine unless severe weather 
 makes it unsafe.\nThe trail is mostly flat and suitable for most fitness l
 evels. Please wear comfortable walking shoes and bring water if it's a war
 m evening.\n\nThis is a **social walk**\, not a guided historical tour. I'
 ll share a little history about the Beltline along the way\, but the focus
  is on enjoying the evening together.\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n
 📍 **Meetup Location:** Outside **Caledonia Station (there is only one e
 xit)**\n🫎 I'll be wearing my Moose Hat.\n⏰ **Meetup Time:** **11:00 A
 M**\n\nI will only wait **5 minutes.**\nEarly is on time.\nOn time is late
 .\nPlease be on time\, as we will leave promptly.\n\n🏁 **End Point:** N
 ear Davisville Station.\n\n***\n\n## 🍽️ After the Walk\n\nWe'll head 
 to **The Bull: A Firkin Pub** for brunch and conversation.\n\n**Menu:** [C
 lick Here!](https://www.firkinpubs.com/thebullandfirkin/menus/)\n\n***\n\n
 ## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$5 cash in person or e-transfer**\n📧 **[math
 ewmaclean@hotmail.com](mailto:mathewmaclean@hotmail.com)**\n\nThis fee hel
 ps support the group and allows us to continue organizing events like this
 . Thank you for supporting community! 💖\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring
 \n\n💧 Water\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🍽️ Money if you'd lik
 e to join us for dinner afterward.\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nT
 his group is open to anyone who wants to be social and make friends—whet
 her single or not.\n\nWe also host:\n🎬 Movies\n🚶 Walks & hikes\n🎭
  Arts & culture outings\n🍽️ Restaurant gatherings\nThere's always som
 ething happening.\n\n***\n\n**REMEMBER:** You're welcome to just show up o
 n the day if you're unsure about your schedule.\nSometimes things happen a
 nd events may need to be cancelled—please keep an eye on updates.\n\n***
 \n\n👤 **Organizer:** Mathew\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email
 :\n📧 **[torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com](mailto:torontomoviesandout
 ings@hotmail.com)**\n\n**Come for the trail.**\n**Stay for the conversatio
 n.**\n\n**Leave wondering how one of Toronto's oldest railway lines became
  one of its best hidden walks.** 🌿🚶‍♂️🍻
