SUMMARY:🔥🌅 GOODBYE SUMMER\, HELLO FALL: TORONTO ISLAND BONFIRE 🌅
 🔥
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!\n# 🔥
 🌅 GOODBYE SUMMER\, HELLO FALL: TORONTO ISLAND BONFIRE 🌅🔥\n\n### F
 ire\, Food\, Music & One Last Summer Night by the Lake\n\nSummer has to en
 d eventually — so why not send it off properly?\nJoin us on **Toronto Is
 land** for an evening bonfire at Olympic Island as we say goodbye to summe
 r and welcome the beginning of fall.\nWe’ll take the ferry across togeth
 er\, settle in by the fire\, enjoy some food and music\, roast marshmallow
 s\, and spend the evening relaxing by the water with the Toronto skyline i
 n the background.\n\nThis isn't a walk.\nIt isn't a tour.\n\nIt's a **soci
 al evening designed to give us time to actually sit around\, talk\, laugh\
 , eat\, and connect with one another.**\nWhether you've been coming to the
  group for years or this is your first event\, this is a chance to slow do
 wn and enjoy the people around you.\n\n📱 Don't forget to join our **Wha
 tsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrK
 Anc)**\n\n***\n\n## 🔥 THE PLAN\n\nWe'll meet at the ferry terminal and 
 take the ferry together to Toronto Island.\nOnce we arrive\, we'll make ou
 r way over to **Olympic Island**\, where our fire pit will be waiting.\n\n
 We'll have:\n🔥 A bonfire\n🌭 Hot dogs — including vegetarian option
 s\n🍡 Marshmallows for roasting\n🎶 Music\n🌆 Beautiful views of the
  Toronto skyline\n🗣️ Plenty of time to sit\, talk and socialize\nThe 
 goal is simple:\n**Come for the fire.**\n**Stay for the food.**\n\n**Leave
  with a few more people you know.** 🔥💛\n\n***\n\n## 🚢 FERRY INFOR
 MATION — PLEASE READ\n\nThe **fall ferry schedule has not been released 
 yet**\, so the ferry departure and return times listed below are **subject
  to change**.\nI will update the event as soon as the official fall schedu
 le is available.\n\n### Current tentative schedule:\n\n📍 **Meetup:** 5:
 15 PM\n🚢 **Ferry:** Approximately 5:30 PM\n🔥 **Bonfire:** Olympic Is
 land\n🚢 **Return ferry:** Approximately 9:00 PM\n\n**Please do not make
  other plans around these ferry times until the fall schedule has been con
 firmed.**\n\nOnce the schedule is released\, the event page will be update
 d with the exact times.\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 MEETUP DETAILS\n\n📍 **Inside 
 the Jack Layton Ferry Terminal\, near the bathrooms**\nYou must enter the 
 ferry terminal and have your ferry ticket **scanned before entering the wa
 iting area**.\nOnce you're inside the terminal\, head toward the **bathroo
 ms**.\n🫎 I'll be wearing my Moose Hat.\n\n**PLEASE BE ON TIME.**\n\nThe
  ferry will not wait for us\, and I will not be able to hold up the group 
 while waiting for late arrivals.\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ FERRY TICKET\n\nYou 
 are responsible for purchasing your own ferry ticket.\n**Ferry fare:** To 
 be confirmed once the fall schedule and current fare are released.\n\n👉
  **[Click Here for Ferry Tickets](https://secure.toronto.ca/FerryTicketOnl
 ine/tickets2/index.jsp)**\n\n***\n\n# 💵 MEETUP FEE — PLEASE READ BEFO
 RE RSVPING\n\nThe meetup fee for this event is **$10**.\nPayment must be m
 ade by **e-transfer to:**\n📧 **mathewmaclean@hotmail.com**\n\n### Payme
 nt is required within 24 hours of signing up.\n\nThis applies to **everyon
 e**.\n\nIt does not matter whether you have been a member for one week\, o
 ne year\, or ten years. It does not matter whether you are a long-standing
  member or a member in good standing.\n**Everyone attending this event pay
 s the $10 meetup fee.**\nThere are no exceptions.\n\nYour payment helps co
 ver:\n🔥 Fire permit\n🪵 Firewood\n🌭 Hot dogs and buns\n🍡 Marshm
 allows\n🎶 Music\n🥄 Shared roasting supplies\n\n**If payment is not r
 eceived within 24 hours\, your RSVP will be removed so someone else can ta
 ke the spot.**\n\n***\n\n## ⚠️ RSVP COMMITMENT\n\nPlease only RSVP if 
 you genuinely intend to attend.\n\n**When you sign up\, you must also answ
 er all of the event questions.**\nThis information helps me plan the food\
 , fire and logistics for the evening.\n\nPlease don't RSVP simply because 
 the event looks interesting and then decide later whether you feel like co
 ming.\n\nIf you aren't sure you can attend\, **please wait until you know 
 before signing up.**\n\nOnce you've committed\, please respect that commit
 ment.\n\n***\n\n## 🍴 WHAT YOUR $10 INCLUDES\n\nYour meetup fee includes
 :\n\n* City permit and fire-related costs\n* Firewood\n* Hot dogs and buns
 \n* Vegetarian hot dog option\n* Sauces and condiments\n* Marshmallows\n* 
 Music\n* Shared roasting sticks\n\n**Bring your own drinks.**\n\n***\n\n##
  🎒 WHAT TO BRING\n\n🥤 Your own drinks\n\n🪑 Folding chair or blank
 et\n🧥 A sweater or jacket — September evenings can get cool\n🍪 Som
 ething small to share if you'd like\n🎲 **A game to share** — bring on
 e along if you'd like and feel free to get a group together to play\n🔥 
 Your own roasting stick if you have one\n📱 Your phone/camera\nDogs are 
 welcome as long as they are well behaved and permitted in the area.\n\n***
 \n\n## 🌧️ WEATHER\n\nThis event is planned as an outdoor bonfire and 
 will happen in most weather conditions.\nIf severe weather or unsafe condi
 tions make the event impossible\, the event may be cancelled or reschedule
 d.\nPlease keep an eye on the event page for updates.\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 TH
 E POINT OF THE EVENING\n\nThis is a social event.\nThe bonfire is really j
 ust the **container**.\nThe important part is what happens around it — s
 itting together\, talking to someone you've never met\, catching up with p
 eople you already know\, sharing food\, laughing\, and maybe making a conn
 ection that continues long after the fire goes out.\nThat's what this grou
 p is really about.\n\nWe also organize:\n🎬 Movies\n🚶 Walks & hikes\n
 🎭 Arts & culture\n🍽️ Restaurant outings\n🎉 Social events\nThere
 's always something happening.\n\n***\n\n👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\nQuest
 ions? Post on the event wall or email:\n📧 **torontomoviesandoutings@hot
 mail.com**\n\n### 🔥 Come for the bonfire.\n\n### 🌭 Stay for the food
 .\n\n### 🌅 Leave with a new connection — and maybe a new friend.\n\n*
 *Let's give summer the send-off it deserves.** 💛🔥
